  "text": "Driving Blender via MCP in Cursor\n\nStar_Knight12 · x · 2026-07-13\n\nA user shared a DIY Blender MCP repository, advising others not to modify it blindly and to consult their preferred LLM or tutorials first. A reply highlighted a practical use case: using GPT-5.6/Sol within Cursor to configure Blender MCP, successfully generating a realistic \"floating MacBook\" render before even opening the Blender UI.\n\nThe key takeaway here isn't Blender itself, but how the LLM + MCP + Cursor stack transforms a highly complex 3D toolchain into an agent-driven workflow.\n\nRelated event: Beginner Runs Blender Rendering via Cursor and MCP(9 posts)→\n\nOriginal post →\n\nMore from coding & agent\n\nAI-built bbtree claims fastest concurrent btree; researcher calls for ambitious academic systems — tianyin_xu · 2026-10-25\n\nOctopus OS: a 45k-line Rust kernel where agents rewrite their own harness mid-task — _AustinCalvert_ · 2026-10-25\n\nDev argues Rust would be better if modules, not crates, were the compilation unit — zetalyrae · 2026-10-25\n\nDev open-sources BizAgent framework where one AI lead agent manages a dozen AI employees — Low-Start2333 · 2026-10-25\n\nFormal Verification Yields to Static Analysis, Which Yields to Better Language Design — xennygrimmato_ · 2026-10-25\n\nScanning 115,798 agent ledger rows: zero capability revocations, none with expiry — Affectionate-Sun265 · 2026-10-25\n\ncoding & agent channel →",
